      "factual_resolution": "Xi_N sends unit-torus/velocity variables to physical(Lx,P0v). For tau0=mL/P0, Xi^-1 Phi_(tau0 s) Xi is a complete smooth flow on Z^N, commutes with label permutations, and differentiates to xprime=v, vprime=(mL/P0^2)N^-1 sumK(L(x_i-x_j))=N^-1 sumk. k(0)=0 permits the selfterm and makes empiricallaw an exact characteristic solution. Positive scalings give no domain/time/unit mismatch. Step1.1 also writes the inner coupling integral explicitly and integrates the two A-Lipschitz distance terms to2A Dx; Gronwall bound unchanged.",
      "disposition": "resolved-in-actual-current-proof"
    },
    {
      "item": "thm-csm-dk-compact-iid-propagation-of-chaos",
      "steps": [
        "3.1"
      ],
      "factual_resolution": "The identical Xi/tau/k scaling is defined before applying the physical finite-N supplier. Its conjugatedflow preserves the iid-induced exchangeability. The already proved initial W1 expectation/almostsure estimates then receive the deterministic e^((1+2A)T) bound uniformly on |s|<=T, with physicaltime tau0s and dimensionless phasevariables explicit. No rate, compact-support, testclass or Choice assumption changes.",
      "disposition": "resolved-in-actual-current-proof"
