      ],
      "factual_resolution": "eta=c chi(2u) has finitepositive normalization, nonnegative unitmass and compact unitsphere support. Its epsilon scaling and locallyfinite periodic lattice sum are independent of representative, smooth, Haar-unitmass and supported within torus distanceepsilon. Product convolution changes a boundedLipschitz test by atmost2epsilonLip; compactvelocity cutoff plusDCT transfers equality. Equality classD of two probabilities containsZ, is complement-closed by equal totalmass and disjoint-union closed by countableadditivity. Closed sets are a generating pi-system for the actual productmetric Borelspace, so Dynkin applies.",
      "disposition": "resolved-in-actual-current-proof"
    },
    {
      "item": "thm-csm-dk-global-lipschitz-vlasov",
      "steps": [
        "6.1"
      ],
      "factual_resolution": "The actual published cutoff construction has sigma=a(t)/(a(t)+a(1-t)) and chi(v)=sigma((4-|v|^2)/3). On0<t<1, the ratio is exp(-1/t+1/(1-t)), whose exponent derivative is1/t^2+1/(1-t)^2>0. sigma is globally nondecreasing withconstant outerpieces, hencechi is radialnonincreasing; chi(v/R) increases to1 asR grows. rho_s>=0 permits MCT, while the pulledback chi_R(V_s)rho0 term is dominated by the probabilitydensityrho0. Thus the normalization/density-identification argument uses a legitimately monotone family.",
      "disposition": "resolved-in-actual-current-proof"
    }
